  "slug": "anisoplanatic-blind-deconvolution-175e",
  "summary": "November 2026 preprints add phase-coded, holographic and deep-learning routes to wavefront recovery through disordered or turbulent media.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is recovering wavefront information in disordered or turbulent optical systems, where spatially varying phase and a field-dependent point-spread function complicate conventional reconstruction. The anisoplanatic blind deconvolution preprint uses a pupil-plane spatial light modulator with known phase codes to jointly recover the image and spatially varying turbulence phases. The holographic-gradient preprint instead obtains the loss gradient from a single off-axis hologram, enabling in situ training of optical systems through disorder. The deep-learning preprint reconstructs multiple wavefronts from one speckle pattern produced by a thin diffuser, using recurrent all-pairs field transforms and Zernike regression. Two of the three preprints rely on single-shot or single-pattern acquisition. All three are preprints, and no quantitative comparison between them is presented here.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
